        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild bilateral conjunctival injection and profuse tearing. Pupils 4–5 mm, equal and reactive; no miosis, ciliary flush, corneal opacity, eyelid oedema, purulent discharge, or foreign body seen on gross examination including lid eversion. Visual acuity approximately 6/9 OU, uncorrected. Extraocular movements full and non-painful. No photophobia."
